WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Luke, Chapter Six.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:12.667
And it came to pass on the second sabbath after the first, that he went through the corn fields; and his disciples plucked the ears of corn, and did eat, rubbing them in their hands.

3
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:19.867
And certain of the Pharisees said unto them, Why do ye that which is not lawful to do on the sabbath days?

4
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:34.400
And Jesus answering them said, Have ye not read so much as this, what David did, when himself was an hungred, and they which were with him; How he went into the house of God, and did take and eat the shewbread, and gave also to them that were with him;

5
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.333
which it is not lawful to eat but for the priests alone?

6
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:42.533
And he said unto them, That the Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.

7
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:50.400
And it came to pass also on another sabbath, that he entered into the synagogue and taught: and there was a man whose right hand was withered.

8
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:57.067
And the scribes and Pharisees watched him, whether he would heal on the sabbath day; that they might find an accusation against him.

9
00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:04.400
But he knew their thoughts, and said to the man which had the withered hand, Rise up, and stand forth in the midst.

10
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.067
And he arose and stood forth.

11
00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:15.467
Then said Jesus unto them, I will ask you one thing; Is it lawful on the sabbath days to do good, or to do evil?

12
00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.867
to save life, or to destroy it?

13
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:23.067
And looking round about upon them all, he said unto the man, Stretch forth thy hand.

14
00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:27.467
And he did so: and his hand was restored whole as the other.

15
00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:32.800
And they were filled with madness; and communed one with another what they might do to Jesus.

16
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.867
And it came to pass in those days, that he went out into a mountain to pray, and continued all night in prayer to God.

17
00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:59.200
And when it was day, he called unto him his disciples: and of them he chose twelve, whom also he named apostles; Simon, (whom he also named Peter,) and Andrew his brother, James and John, Philip and Bartholomew, Matthew and Thomas, James the son of Alphaeus, and Simon called Zelotes,

18
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.000
And Judas the brother of James, and Judas Iscariot, which also was the traitor.

19
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:20.800
And he came down with them, and stood in the plain, and the company of his disciples, and a great multitude of people out of all Judaea and Jerusalem, and from the sea coast of Tyre and Sidon, which came to hear him, and to be healed of their diseases; And they that were vexed with unclean spirits:

20
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.133
and they were healed.

21
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:28.000
And the whole multitude sought to touch him: for there went virtue out of him, and healed them all.

22
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.267
And he lifted up his eyes on his disciples, and said, Blessed be ye poor: for yours is the kingdom of God.

23
00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:38.267
Blessed are ye that hunger now: for ye shall be filled.

24
00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:41.867
Blessed are ye that weep now: for ye shall laugh.

25
00:02:41.867 --> 00:02:52.267
Blessed are ye, when men shall hate you, and when they shall separate you from their company, and shall reproach you, and cast out your name as evil, for the Son of man's sake.

26
00:02:52.267 --> 00:03:01.867
Rejoice ye in that day, and leap for joy: for, behold, your reward is great in heaven: for in the like manner did their fathers unto the prophets.

27
00:03:01.867 --> 00:03:04.267
But woe unto you that are rich!

28
00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.400
for ye have received your consolation.

29
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.267
Woe unto you that are full!

30
00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.467
for ye shall hunger.

31
00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:11.467
Woe unto you that laugh now!

32
00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.467
for ye shall mourn and weep.

33
00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:16.933
Woe unto you, when all men shall speak well of you!

34
00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:19.733
for so did their fathers to the false prophets.

35
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:29.333
But I say unto you which hear, Love your enemies, do good to them which hate you, Bless them that curse you, and pray for them which despitefully use you.

36
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:37.333
And unto him that smiteth thee on the one cheek offer also the other; and him that taketh away thy cloke forbid not to take thy coat also.

37
00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:43.867
Give to every man that asketh of thee; and of him that taketh away thy goods ask them not again.

38
00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:48.667
And as ye would that men should do to you, do ye also to them likewise.

39
00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:52.800
For if ye love them which love you, what thank have ye?

40
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.400
for sinners also love those that love them.

41
00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.667
And if ye do good to them which do good to you, what thank have ye?

42
00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.333
for sinners also do even the same.

43
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:07.467
And if ye lend to them of whom ye hope to receive, what thank have ye?

44
00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:11.467
for sinners also lend to sinners, to receive as much again.

45
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:24.133
But love ye your enemies, and do good, and lend, hoping for nothing again; and your reward shall be great, and ye shall be the children of the Highest: for he is kind unto the unthankful and to the evil.

46
00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:28.400
Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.

47
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:44.800
Judge not, and ye shall not be judged: condemn not, and ye shall not be condemned: forgive, and ye shall be forgiven: Give, and it shall be given unto you; good measure, pressed down, and shaken together, and running over, shall men give into your bosom.

48
00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.333
For with the same measure that ye mete withal it shall be measured to you again.

49
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:53.333
And he spake a parable unto them, Can the blind lead the blind?

50
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:56.133
shall they not both fall into the ditch?

51
00:04:56.133 --> 00:05:02.133
The disciple is not above his master: but every one that is perfect shall be as his master.

52
00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:09.067
And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother's eye, but perceivest not the beam that is in thine own eye?

53
00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:18.400
Either how canst thou say to thy brother, Brother, let me pull out the mote that is in thine eye, when thou thyself beholdest not the beam that is in thine own eye?

54
00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:26.667
Thou hypocrite, cast out first the beam out of thine own eye, and then shalt thou see clearly to pull out the mote that is in thy brother's eye.

55
00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:32.133
For a good tree bringeth not forth corrupt fruit; neither doth a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.

56
00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.667
For every tree is known by his own fruit.

57
00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:39.467
For of thorns men do not gather figs, nor of a bramble bush gather they grapes.

58
00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:51.733
A good man out of the good treasure of his heart bringeth forth that which is good; and an evil man out of the evil treasure of his heart bringeth forth that which is evil: for of the abundance of the heart his mouth speaketh.

59
00:05:51.733 --> 00:05:56.133
And why call ye me, Lord, Lord, and do not the things which I say?

60
00:05:56.133 --> 00:06:12.800
Whosoever cometh to me, and heareth my sayings, and doeth them, I will shew you to whom he is like: He is like a man which built an house, and digged deep, and laid the foundation on a rock: and when the flood arose, the stream beat vehemently upon that house, and could not shake it:

61
00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.800
for it was founded upon a rock.

62
00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:27.200
But he that heareth, and doeth not, is like a man that without a foundation built an house upon the earth; against which the stream did beat vehemently, and immediately it fell; and the ruin of that house was great.

